// A missing `}` does not produce one error at the missing brace: it produces a
// cascade at tokens the parser then misreads as something else. The `}` the
// author meant for `class Decision` is never written, so `rule` and `start` are
// read as a field and its type, `when` starts a presence condition, and the `=>`
// is what finally fails — three errors, none of them about a delimiter. Each one
// now names a bracket the file genuinely leaves open.
//
// That bracket is the WORKFLOW's, not the class's, and the difference is the
// whole point. Counting brackets, the class's `{` IS closed — by the `}` on the
// last line, which the author wrote for the workflow. Only the workflow's `{` is
// provably unmatched, so only it can be named: a note that calls a block open
// when it is closed tells the reader to add a brace they already wrote.
workflow UnclosedBrace {
  class Decision {
    ok bool

  rule start
    when Started
    => {
      complete { ok true }
    }
}
